                <pb facs="0366" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg282"/>

                <head>No. 135.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Señor Flores.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Wilmington, Del.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-07-04"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 4,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Understanding from your announcement of amnesty that Santos is now at liberty to
                    come home, the Iroquois will be recalled.</p>
                <p>Show this to Mr. Adee.</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
